{"id":"mahabharata-12-271","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":271,"title":"एकसप्तत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 271 · Vritra's knowledge of Vishnu","summary":{"en":"Vritra, praised by Ushanas for his knowledge, bows to the god Vishnu from whom came the earth and sky, and tells of Vishnu in the forms of the qualities. He is told how the soul passes among the six stages of colour from the dark to the white, and of the way of the high Brahman.","kn":"ಉಶನಸನಿಂದ ಜ್ಞಾನಕ್ಕಾಗಿ ಹೊಗಳಲ್ಪಟ್ಟ ವೃತ್ರ ಭೂಮಿ-ಆಕಾಶ ಹುಟ್ಟಿದ ವಿಷ್ಣುವಿಗೆ ನಮಿಸಿ ಗುಣರೂಪದ ವಿಷ್ಣುವನ್ನು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಆತ್ಮ ಕಪ್ಪಿನಿಂದ ಬಿಳುಪಿನವರೆಗೆ ಆರು ವರ್ಣ ಹಂತಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಸಾಗುವುದು, ಪರಬ್ರಹ್ಮದ ಮಾರ್ಗ ಹೇಳಲ್ಪಡುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"उशना से ज्ञान के लिए प्रशंसित वृत्र उन विष्णु को नमन करता है जिनसे पृथ्वी और आकाश उपजे और गुणरूप विष्णु का वर्णन करता है। उसे बताया जाता है कि जीव काले से श्वेत तक छह वर्ण-स्तरों से कैसे गुजरता है और परब्रह्म का मार्ग क्या है।","te":"ఉశనసునిచే జ్ఞానానికి ప్రశంసింపబడిన వృత్రుడు భూమి ఆకాశాలు పుట్టిన విష్ణువుకు నమస్కరించి గుణరూప విష్ణువును వర్ణిస్తాడు. జీవుడు నలుపు నుండి తెలుపు వరకు ఆరు వర్ణ స్థాయిలను దాటే తీరు, పరబ్రహ్మ మార్గం చెప్పబడతాయి.","ta":"உசனஸால் அறிவுக்காகப் புகழப்பட்ட வித்ரன் நிலமும் வானமும் தோன்றிய விஷ்ணுவை வணங்கிக் குணவடிவ விஷ்ணுவை விவரிக்கிறான். ஆன்மா கருமையிலிருந்து வெண்மைவரை ஆறு நிற நிலைகளைக் கடக்கும் விதமும் பரப்பிரம்ம வழியும் கூறப்படுகின்றன.","ml":"ജ്ഞാനത്തിന് ഉശനസ്സ് പ്രശംസിച്ച വൃത്രൻ, ഭൂമിയും ആകാശവും ഉണ്ടാക്കിയ വിഷ്ണുവിനെ നമസ്കരിക്കുന്നു; ഗുണങ്ങളുടെ രൂപങ്ങളിലുള്ള വിഷ്ണുവിനെക്കുറിച്ച് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. കറുപ്പിൽനിന്ന് വെളുപ്പിലേക്കുള്ള ആറു വർണ്ണ ഘട്ടങ്ങളിലൂടെ ആത്മാവ് കടന്നുപോകുന്നതെങ്ങനെയെന്നും, ഉന്നതബ്രഹ്മത്തിലേക്കുള്ള വഴിയും അദ്ദേഹത്തെ പഠിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.271; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"उशनोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Ushanas said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"नमस्तस्मै भगवते देवाय प्रभविष्णवे ।\nयस्य पृथ्वीतलं तात साकाशं बाहुगोचरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Homage to that blessed god, the all-powerful, whose arms reach the surface of the earth together with the sky."}},{"n":2,"text":"मूर्धा यस्य त्वनन्तं च स्थानं दानवसत्तम ।\nतस्याहं ते प्रवक्ष्यामि विष्णोर्माहात्म्यमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose head is the endless, best of the Danavas: I will tell you the supreme greatness of that Vishnu."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"तयोः संवदतोरेवमाजगाम महामुनिः ।\nसनत्कुमारो धर्मात्मा संशयच्छेदनाय वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"While they were speaking thus, the great sage Sanatkumara, righteous in soul, came to cut their doubt."}},{"n":4,"text":"स पूजितोऽसुरेन्द्रेण मुनिनोशनसा तथा ।\nनिषसादासने राजन्महार्हे मुनिपुंगवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honored by the lord of the asuras and by the sage Ushanas, that bull among sages sat on a very worthy seat, O king."}},{"n":5,"text":"तमासीनं महाप्राज्ञमुशना वाक्यमब्रवीत् ।\nब्रूह्यस्मै दानवेन्द्राय विष्णोर्माहात्म्यमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"To him seated, very wise, Ushanas said: \"Tell this lord of the Danavas the supreme greatness of Vishnu.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"सनत्कुमारस्तु ततः श्रुत्वा प्राह वचोऽर्थवत् ।\nविष्णोर्माहात्म्यसंयुक्तं दानवेन्द्राय धीमते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Sanatkumara, having heard, spoke meaningful words, full of Vishnu's greatness, to the wise lord of the Danavas."}},{"n":7,"text":"शृणु सर्वमिदं दैत्य विष्णोर्माहात्म्यमुत्तमम् ।\nविष्णौ जगत्स्थितं सर्वमिति विद्धि परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hear all this, Daitya, the supreme greatness of Vishnu. Know, scorcher of foes, that the whole world rests in Vishnu."}},{"n":8,"text":"सृजत्येष महाबाहो भूतग्रामं चराचरम् ।\nएष चाक्षिपते काले काले विसृजते पुनः ।\nअस्मिन्गच्छन्ति विलयमस्माच्च प्रभवन्त्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"He creates, mighty-armed, the whole host of beings, moving and unmoving. In time he draws them in, and in time lets them go again. In him they dissolve, and from him they arise."}},{"n":9,"text":"नैष दानवता शक्यस्तपसा नैव चेज्यया ।\nसंप्राप्तुमिन्द्रियाणां तु संयमेनैव शक्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He cannot be reached by demonhood, nor by austerity or sacrifice; he can be reached only by restraint of the senses."}},{"n":10,"text":"बाह्ये चाभ्यन्तरे चैव कर्मणा मनसि स्थितः ।\nनिर्मलीकुरुते बुद्ध्या सोऽमुत्रानन्त्यमश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who stands in mind, in outer and inner action, cleanses himself by understanding and gains endlessness hereafter."}},{"n":11,"text":"यथा हिरण्यकर्ता वै रूप्यमग्नौ विशोधयेत् ।\nबहुशोऽतिप्रयत्नेन महतात्मकृतेन ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a goldsmith purifies silver in fire many times with great effort made by himself,"}},{"n":12,"text":"तद्वज्जातिशतैर्जीवः शुध्यतेऽल्पेन कर्मणा ।\nयत्नेन महता चैवाप्येकजातौ विशुध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"so a soul is purified over a hundred births by small action, or with great effort in a single birth."}},{"n":13,"text":"लीलयाल्पं यथा गात्रात्प्रमृज्यादात्मनो रजः ।\nबहु यत्नेन महता दोषनिर्हरणं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As one easily wipes a little dust from one's body, yet removing faults takes great effort,"}},{"n":14,"text":"यथा चाल्पेन माल्येन वासितं तिलसर्षपम् ।\nन मुञ्चति स्वकं गन्धं तद्वत्सूक्ष्मस्य दर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and as sesame or mustard scented with a few flowers does not give up its own smell, so is the vision of the subtle."}},{"n":15,"text":"तदेव बहुभिर्माल्यैर्वास्यमानं पुनः पुनः ।\nविमुञ्चति स्वकं गन्धं माल्यगन्धेऽवतिष्ठति ॥","meaning":{"en":"But when scented with many flowers again and again, it gives up its own smell and keeps the flowers' scent."}},{"n":16,"text":"एवं जातिशतैर्युक्तो गुणैरेव प्रसङ्गिषु ।\nबुद्ध्या निवर्तते दोषो यत्नेनाभ्यासजेन वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus, over a hundred births, through virtues themselves among those attached, the fault is turned back by understanding and by effort born of practice."}},{"n":17,"text":"कर्मणा स्वेन रक्तानि विरक्तानि च दानव ।\nयथा कर्मविशेषांश्च प्राप्नुवन्ति तथा शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Danava, hear how beings, attached and detached by their own action, reach the different results of action."}},{"n":18,"text":"यथा च संप्रवर्तन्ते यस्मिंस्तिष्ठन्ति वा विभो ।\nतत्तेऽनुपूर्व्या व्याख्यास्ये तदिहैकमनाः शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"How they proceed and where they stand, lord, I will explain in order; listen here with one mind."}},{"n":19,"text":"अनादिनिधनः श्रीमान्हरिर्नारायणः प्रभुः ।\nस वै सृजति भूतानि स्थावराणि चराणि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hari Narayana, the lord, glorious, without beginning or end, creates beings, standing and moving."}},{"n":20,"text":"एष सर्वेषु भूतेषु क्षरश्चाक्षर एव च ।\nएकादशविकारात्मा जगत्पिबति रश्मिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He is, in all beings, both the perishable and the imperishable; with eleven modifications as his self, he drinks the world with his rays."}},{"n":21,"text":"पादौ तस्य महीं विद्धि मूर्धानं दिवमेव च ।\nबाहवस्तु दिशो दैत्य श्रोत्रमाकाशमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know the earth as his feet and the sky as his head; the quarters are his arms, Daitya, and space is his hearing."}},{"n":22,"text":"तस्य तेजोमयः सूर्यो मनश्चन्द्रमसि स्थितम् ।\nबुद्धिर्ज्ञानगता नित्यं रसस्त्वप्सु प्रवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"His is the sun, made of radiance; the mind abides in the moon; understanding is ever in knowledge; flavor moves in the waters."}},{"n":23,"text":"भ्रुवोरनन्तरास्तस्य ग्रहा दानवसत्तम ।\nनक्षत्रचक्रं नेत्राभ्यां पादयोर्भूश्च दानव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The planets lie between his brows, best of Danavas; the wheel of stars is in his eyes, and the earth in his feet."}},{"n":24,"text":"रजस्तमश्च सत्त्वं च विद्धि नारायणात्मकम् ।\nसोऽऽश्रमाणां मुखं तात कर्मणस्तत्फलं विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know passion, darkness and goodness as made of Narayana. He is the mouth of the stages of life; they know the fruit of action as his."}},{"n":25,"text":"अकर्मणः फलं चैव स एव परमव्ययः ।\nछन्दांसि तस्य रोमाणि अक्षरं च सरस्वती ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fruit of non-action too is that same supreme imperishable. The meters are his hair, and the imperishable word is Sarasvati."}},{"n":26,"text":"बह्वाश्रयो बहुमुखो धर्मो हृदि समाश्रितः ।\nस ब्रह्मपरमो धर्मस्तपश्च सदसच्च सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dharma, with many supports and many faces, rests in his heart. He is supreme Brahman, dharma, austerity, and being and non-being."}},{"n":27,"text":"श्रुतिशास्त्रग्रहोपेतः षोडशर्त्विक्क्रतुश्च सः ।\nपितामहश्च विष्णुश्च सोऽश्विनौ स पुरंदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Endowed with scripture, treatise and the planets, he is the sixteen-priest sacrifice. He is Brahma and Vishnu, the Ashvins and Purandara."}},{"n":28,"text":"मित्रश्च वरुणश्चैव यमोऽथ धनदस्तथा ।\nते पृथग्दर्शनास्तस्य संविदन्ति तथैकताम् ।\nएकस्य विद्धि देवस्य सर्वं जगदिदं वशे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mitra, Varuna, Yama and Kubera: they see him separately and yet agree in his oneness. Know that this whole world is in the power of one god."}},{"n":29,"text":"नानाभूतस्य दैत्येन्द्र तस्यैकत्वं वदत्ययम् ।\nजन्तुः पश्यति ज्ञानेन ततः सत्त्वं प्रकाशते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of him who has become many, lord of Daityas, this speaks of his unity; a creature sees it by knowledge, and then goodness shines."}},{"n":30,"text":"संहारविक्षेपसहस्रकोटी-\nस्तिष्ठन्ति जीवाः प्रचरन्ति चान्ये ।\nप्रजाविसर्गस्य च पारिमाण्यं\nवापीसहस्राणि बहूनि दैत्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thousands of crores of dissolutions and emissions stand; some souls remain and others go forth. The measure of creation of creatures is like many thousands of lakes, Daitya."}},{"n":31,"text":"वाप्यः पुनर्योजनविस्तृतास्ताः\nक्रोशं च गम्भीरतयावगाढाः ।\nआयामतः पञ्चशताश्च सर्वाः\nप्रत्येकशो योजनतः प्रवृद्धाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those lakes are each a yojana wide, a krosha deep, five hundred in length, and each grows by a yojana."}},{"n":32,"text":"वाप्या जलं क्षिप्यति वालकोट्या\nत्वह्ना सकृच्चाप्यथ न द्वितीयम् ।\nतासां क्षये विद्धि कृतं विसर्गं\nसंहारमेकं च तथा प्रजानाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If one hair-tip's crore of water is taken from a lake once in a day, and not a second time, know that when the lakes are exhausted one creation and one dissolution of creatures is done."}},{"n":33,"text":"षड्जीववर्णाः परमं प्रमाणं\nकृष्णो धूम्रो नीलमथास्य मध्यम् ।\nरक्तं पुनः सह्यतरं सुखं तु\nहारिद्रवर्णं सुसुखं च शुक्लम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The six colors of the soul are the highest measure: black, smoke-colored, and blue in the middle; red is more bearable and pleasant; turmeric-colored very pleasant, and white."}},{"n":34,"text":"परं तु शुक्लं विमलं विशोकं\nगतक्लमं सिध्यति दानवेन्द्र ।\nगत्वा तु योनिप्रभवानि दैत्य\nसहस्रशः सिद्धिमुपैति जीवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the highest white, spotless and sorrowless, free of weariness, leads to success, lord of Danavas. Having gone through wombs by the thousand, Daitya, the soul attains success."}},{"n":35,"text":"गतिं च यां दर्शनमाह देवो\nगत्वा शुभं दर्शनमेव चाह ।\nगतिः पुनर्वर्णकृता प्रजानां\nवर्णस्तथा कालकृतोऽसुरेन्द्र ॥","meaning":{"en":"The goal that the god declares for vision, having gone, he declares the vision good; the goal of creatures is made by color, and color by time, lord of asuras."}},{"n":36,"text":"शतं सहस्राणि चतुर्दशेह\nपरा गतिर्जीवगुणस्य दैत्य ।\nआरोहणं तत्कृतमेव विद्धि\nस्थानं तथा निःसरणं च तेषाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A hundred thousand and fourteen here is the highest course of the soul's quality, Daitya. Know that ascent is made by that, and the stay and departure of beings."}},{"n":37,"text":"कृष्णस्य वर्णस्य गतिर्निकृष्टा\nस मज्जते नरके पच्यमानः ।\nस्थानं तथा दुर्गतिभिस्तु तस्य\nप्रजाविसर्गान्सुबहून्वदन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the black color the goal is lowest; he sinks in hell, cooked; and for his place with evil fates they say there are very many creations of creatures."}},{"n":38,"text":"शतं सहस्राणि ततश्चरित्वा\nप्राप्नोति वर्णं हरितं तु पश्चात् ।\nस चैव तस्मिन्निवसत्यनीशो\nयुगक्षये तमसा संवृतात्मा ॥","meaning":{"en":"After wandering a hundred thousand he gets the green color afterward, and he lives there without mastery, his self covered with darkness until the end of the age."}},{"n":39,"text":"स वै यदा सत्त्वगुणेन युक्त-\nस्तमो व्यपोहन्घटते स्वबुद्ध्या ।\nस लोहितं वर्णमुपैति नीलो\nमनुष्यलोके परिवर्तते च ॥","meaning":{"en":"When, joined with the quality of goodness, he strives by his own understanding to drive off darkness, he attains the red color from blue and turns in the world of men."}},{"n":40,"text":"स तत्र संहारविसर्गमेव\nस्वकर्मजैर्बन्धनैः क्लिश्यमानः ।\nततः स हारिद्रमुपैति वर्णं\nसंहारविक्षेपशते व्यतीते ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, afflicted by bonds born of his own actions, he goes through dissolution and emission; then, after a hundred dissolutions and emissions pass, he reaches the turmeric color."}},{"n":41,"text":"हारिद्रवर्णस्तु प्रजाविसर्गा-\nन्सहस्रशस्तिष्ठति संचरन्वै ।\nअविप्रमुक्तो निरये च दैत्य\nततः सहस्राणि दशापराणि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Turmeric-colored, he moves through thousands of creations of creatures, not fully freed, Daitya, and in hell, then ten thousand more."}},{"n":42,"text":"गतीः सहस्राणि च पञ्च तस्य\nचत्वारि संवर्तकृतानि चैव ।\nविमुक्तमेनं निरयाच्च विद्धि\nसर्वेषु चान्येषु च संभवेषु ॥","meaning":{"en":"His courses are five thousand and four made by the great dissolution; know him freed from hell and in all other births."}},{"n":43,"text":"स देवलोके विहरत्यभीक्ष्णं\nततश्च्युतो मानुषतामुपैति ।\nसंहारविक्षेपशतानि चाष्टौ\nमर्त्येषु तिष्ठन्नमृतत्वमेति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He plays constantly in the world of the gods, and falling from there becomes human. Remaining eight hundred dissolutions and emissions among mortals, he reaches immortality."}},{"n":44,"text":"सोऽस्मादथ भ्रश्यति कालयोगा-\nत्कृष्णे तले तिष्ठति सर्वकष्टे ।\nयथा त्वयं सिध्यति जीवलोक-\nस्तत्तेऽभिधास्याम्यसुरप्रवीर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he falls from this, by the force of time, and stays in the black lower level full of every suffering. How this world of souls is perfected I will tell you, hero among asuras."}},{"n":45,"text":"दैवानि स व्यूहशतानि सप्त\nरक्तो हरिद्रोऽथ तथैव शुक्लः ।\nसंश्रित्य संधावति शुक्लमेत-\nमष्टापरानर्च्यतमान्स लोकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Red, turmeric, and likewise white: relying on these, he runs through seven hundred divine arrangements, and then reaches this white and eight more worlds worthy of worship."}},{"n":46,"text":"अष्टौ च षष्टिं च शतानि यानि\nमनोविरुद्धानि महाद्युतीनाम् ।\nशुक्लस्य वर्णस्य परा गतिर्या\nत्रीण्येव रुद्धानि महानुभाव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The eight and sixty hundreds that the great radiant ones hold in mind opposed: the highest goal of the white color has only three barred."}},{"n":47,"text":"संहारविक्षेपमनिष्टमेकं\nचत्वारि चान्यानि वसत्यनीशः ।\nषष्ठस्य वर्णस्य परा गतिर्या\nसिद्धा विशिष्टस्य गतक्लमस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"One unwanted dissolution and emission, and four others, he lives without mastery. The highest goal of the sixth color, of the distinguished and weariless, is success."}},{"n":48,"text":"सप्तोत्तरं तेषु वसत्यनीशः\nसंहारविक्षेपशतं सशेषम् ।\nतस्मादुपावृत्य मनुष्यलोके\nततो महान्मानुषतामुपैति ॥","meaning":{"en":"In those he lives without mastery for a hundred and seven dissolutions and emissions with a remainder; turning back from that into the world of men, then, great, he reaches humanity."}},{"n":49,"text":"तस्मादुपावृत्य ततः क्रमेण\nसोऽग्रे स्म संतिष्ठति भूतसर्गम् ।\nस सप्तकृत्वश्च परैति लोका-\nन्संहारविक्षेपकृतप्रवासः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Turning back from that in order, he stands first at the creation of beings; seven times he goes to worlds, living away through dissolutions and emissions."}},{"n":50,"text":"सप्तैव संहारमुपप्लवानि\nसंभाव्य संतिष्ठति सिद्धलोके ।\nततोऽव्ययं स्थानमनन्तमेति\nदेवस्य विष्णोरथ ब्रह्मणश्च ।\nशेषस्य चैवाथ नरस्य चैव\nदेवस्य विष्णोः परमस्य चैव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having endured seven dissolutions and floods, he stands in the world of the perfected. Then he reaches the imperishable, endless abode of the god Vishnu and Brahma, of Shesha and the man, and of Vishnu the supreme."}},{"n":51,"text":"संहारकाले परिदग्धकाया\nब्रह्माणमायान्ति सदा प्रजा हि ।\nचेष्टात्मनो देवगणाश्च सर्वे\nये ब्रह्मलोकादमराः स्म तेऽपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the time of dissolution, creatures with burnt bodies always come to Brahma; the active-minded hosts of gods too, who were immortals from Brahma's world."}},{"n":52,"text":"प्रजाविसर्गं तु सशेषकालं\nस्थानानि स्वान्येव सरन्ति जीवाः ।\nनिःशेषाणां तत्पदं यान्ति चान्ते\nसर्वापदा ये सदृशा मनुष्याः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the creation of creatures with time left over, souls go to their own places; at the end they go to the abode of those without remainder, the men who are like them in all calamities."}},{"n":53,"text":"ये तु च्युताः सिद्धलोकात्क्रमेण\nतेषां गतिं यान्ति तथानुपूर्व्या ।\nजीवाः परे तद्बलवेषरूपा\nविधिं स्वकं यान्ति विपर्ययेण ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who have fallen in order from the world of the perfected go the course of those, in sequence; other souls, with their strength, dress and form, go by reversal to their own rule."}},{"n":54,"text":"स यावदेवास्ति सशेषभुक्ते\nप्रजाश्च देव्यौ च तथैव शुक्ले ।\nतावत्तदा तेषु विशुद्धभावः\nसंयम्य पञ्चेन्द्रियरूपमेतत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As long as there is a remainder to be enjoyed, creatures and two goddesses remain in the white; so long there, of pure disposition, restraining these five sense forms,"}},{"n":55,"text":"शुद्धां गतिं तां परमां परैति\nशुद्धेन नित्यं मनसा विचिन्वन् ।\nततोऽव्ययं स्थानमुपैति ब्रह्म\nदुष्प्रापमभ्येति स शाश्वतं वै ।\nइत्येतदाख्यातमहीनसत्त्व\nनारायणस्येह बलं मया ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"he goes to that highest pure goal, always inquiring with pure mind. Then he reaches the imperishable abode, Brahman, hard to reach, the eternal. Thus the strength of Narayana, of undiminished power, has been told to you here by me."}},{"text":"वृत्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vritra said:"}},{"n":56,"text":"एवं गते मे न विषादोऽस्ति कश्चि-\nत्सम्यक्च पश्यामि वचस्तवैतत् ।\nश्रुत्वा च ते वाचमदीनसत्त्व\nविकल्मषोऽस्म्यद्य तथा विपाप्मा ॥","meaning":{"en":"This being so, I have no despair at all, and I see your words rightly. Having heard your speech, of undismayed strength, I am today free of stain and sin."}},{"n":57,"text":"प्रवृत्तमेतद्भगवन्महर्षे\nमहाद्युतेश्चक्रमनन्तवीर्यम् ।\nविष्णोरनन्तस्य सनातनं त-\nत्स्थानं सर्गा यत्र सर्वे प्रवृत्ताः ।\nस वै महात्मा पुरुषोत्तमो वै\nतस्मिञ्जगत्सर्वमिदं प्रतिष्ठितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This wheel of the great-radiant, endlessly powerful Vishnu, great sage, is set in motion; and that is the eternal abode where all creations proceed. He is truly the great Supreme Person; in him all this world is established."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":58,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा स कौन्तेय वृत्रः प्राणानवासृजत् ।\nयोजयित्वा तथात्मानं परं स्थानमवाप्तवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, son of Kunti, Vritra gave up his life; uniting himself, he reached the highest place."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":59,"text":"अयं स भगवान्देवः पितामह जनार्दनः ।\nसनत्कुमारो वृत्राय यत्तदाख्यातवान्पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Grandfather, is this the blessed god Janardana, of whom Sanatkumara told Vritra long ago?"}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":60,"text":"मूलस्थायी स भगवान्स्वेनानन्तेन तेजसा ।\nतत्स्थः सृजति तान्भावान्नानारूपान्महातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That blessed one, abiding at the root with his own endless radiance and standing there, creates beings of many forms, he of great austerity."}},{"n":61,"text":"तुरीयार्धेन तस्येमं विद्धि केशवमच्युतम् ।\nतुरीयार्धेन लोकांस्त्रीन्भावयत्येष बुद्धिमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know this Keshava, Achyuta, as a fourth part of his half; with a fourth part the wise one makes the three worlds come to be."}},{"n":62,"text":"अर्वाक्स्थितस्तु यः स्थायी कल्पान्ते परिवर्तते ।\nस शेते भगवानप्सु योऽसावतिबलः प्रभुः ।\nतान्विधाता प्रसन्नात्मा लोकांश्चरति शाश्वतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lower-standing one who stays and turns at the end of the age, the blessed all-powerful lord, sleeps in the waters. The creator, with a gracious soul, moves among the eternal worlds."}},{"n":63,"text":"सर्वाण्यशून्यानि करोत्यनन्तः\nसनत्कुमारः संचरते च लोकान् ।\nस चानिरुद्धः सृजते महात्मा\nतत्स्थं जगत्सर्वमिदं विचित्रम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Endless makes all things not empty; Sanatkumara moves through the worlds. And the great-souled Aniruddha creates; all this varied world stands in him."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":64,"text":"वृत्रेण परमार्थज्ञ दृष्टा मन्येऽऽत्मनो गतिः ।\nशुभा तस्मात्स सुखितो न शोचति पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knower of the highest truth, I think Vritra saw his own good goal; therefore he is happy and does not grieve, grandfather."}},{"n":65,"text":"शुक्लः शुक्लाभिजातीयः साध्यो नावर्ततेऽनघ ।\nतिर्यग्गतेश्च निर्मुक्तो निरयाच्च पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"The white one, born of white origin, perfected, does not return, sinless one, grandfather, being freed from animal birth and hell."}},{"n":66,"text":"हारिद्रवर्णे रक्ते वा वर्तमानस्तु पार्थिव ।\nतिर्यगेवानुपश्येत कर्मभिस्तामसैर्वृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king in the turmeric or red color sees only an animal birth, covered by dark deeds."}},{"n":67,"text":"वयं तु भृशमापन्ना रक्ताः कष्टमुखेऽसुखे ।\nकां गतिं प्रतिपत्स्यामो नीलां कृष्णाधमामथ ॥","meaning":{"en":"But we are greatly afflicted, red, at the mouth of hardship and unhappiness. What goal will we gain, the blue, or the lowest, black?"}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":68,"text":"शुद्धाभिजनसंपन्नाः पाण्डवाः संशितव्रताः ।\nविहृत्य देवलोकेषु पुनर्मानुष्यमेष्यथ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas, endowed with pure lineage and firm vows, after roaming the worlds of the gods will come again as men."}},{"n":69,"text":"प्रजाविसर्गं च सुखेन काले\nप्रत्येत्य देवेषु सुखानि भुक्त्वा ।\nसुखेन संयास्यथ सिद्धसंख्यां\nमा वो भयं भूद्विमलाः स्थ सर्वे ॥","meaning":{"en":"After the creation of beings, happily in time, having enjoyed pleasures among the gods, you will go happily to the company of the perfected. Let no fear be yours; you are all spotless."}}]}]}